# A download still in progress can be paused, resumed and cancelled from its row's menu (GitHub
# #272). ${TRICKLE} sends the first 64 KB of a 10 MB file and holds the rest, so the download
# stays in progress until the scenario cancels it; cancelled, nothing is left running for the
# quit at the end (which would otherwise ask "Downloads in progress").
# promise: #272
home
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/trickle.bin
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=started
expect-log download state started: running=true progress=0.007 rows=\["66 KB of 10 MB
cra://debug?download=pause
expect-log download control: pause
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadState=paused
expect-log download state paused: running=true progress=0.007 rows=\["Paused"\]
cra://debug?download=resume
expect-log download control: resume
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadState=resumed
expect-log download state resumed: running=true progress=0.007 rows=\["66 KB of 10 MB
cra://debug?download=cancel
expect-log download control: cancel
wait 1
cra://debug?downloadState=cancelled
expect-log download state cancelled: running=false progress=none rows=\["Cancelled"\]
